  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Acer palmatum dissectum 'Dr. Brown' Deep Red Dwarf Weeping Japanese Maple Zones 5-9 'Dr. Brown' has earned a degree in its beauty. Dr. Brown has a heavily ornamental leaf that often has more lobes that most other laceleafs. The color is a soft pinkish brown that has an overall look of unique shade of soft maroon. This laceleaf is unique and is a favorite among those who try this beauty out. Dr Brown can reach 4 ft in height by 5 ft in width in 10 years. The overall habit is cascading, forming a nice umbrella. In autumn, Dr Brown puts on a display of yellows, oranges and reds . Make sure to make this tree a focal point in your garden! The photo(s) with a MrMaple logo are owned by MrMaple.com and cannot be used without expressed written consent. The photos on this page without a MrMaple logo were taken by Talon Buchholz and cannot be used without expressed written consent from the owner."
  },
